  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Deloitte Consulting obligated $2.9B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Deloitte Consulting received 644 awards with an average award size of $4.5M, and obligations fell 2.8% year over year. Yearly obligations show a trend of growth through FY24 then a partial pullback: FY21 was $2.4B, FY22 was $2.6B, FY23 was $2.9B, FY24 was $3.3B, FY25 was $3B, and FY26 was $2.9B. The General Services Administration is the largest buyer, obligating $893M, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services at $445M and the Department of Veterans Affairs at $425M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market by NAICS at $1.3B, followed by Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $659M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $372M. Other notable markets include Engineering Services at $275M and a range of specialized services from Automotive Body, Paint, and Interior Repair and Maintenance at $33.2M to Human Resources Consulting Services at $24.1M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Deloitte Consulting's largest federal customers?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration is Deloitte Consulting's largest customer, obligating $893M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $445M and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $425M. The Department of Defense obligated $411M, and the Departments of Homeland Security, State, Treasury, Energy, Commerce, and Agriculture follow with obligations ranging from $257M down to $34.8M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What services and markets drive Deloitte Consulting's federal revenue?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market, accounting for $1.3B in obligations. Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services follows at $659M, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences accounts for $372M. Engineering Services accounts for $275M, with other professional and technical services and niche categories contributing amounts from $82.8M down to $24.1M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Deloitte Consulting make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Deloitte Consulting obligated $2.9B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Deloitte Consulting received 644 awards with an average award size of $4.5M, and obligations fell 2.8% year over year. Historical yearly obligations were $2.4B in FY21, $2.6B in FY22, $2.9B in FY23, $3.3B in FY24, and $3B in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Deloitte Consulting?",
      "a": "The General Services Administration is Deloitte Consulting's top buyer, obligating $893M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $445M and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $425M. The Department of Defense obligated $411M and departments including Homeland Security, State, Treasury, Energy, Commerce, and Agriculture also purchased services."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Deloitte Consulting sell to the government?",
      "a": "Deloitte Consulting sells a mix of IT, management consulting, R&D, and engineering services to the government. Computer Systems Design Services generated $1.3B, Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services generated $659M, Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences generated $372M, and Engineering Services generated $275M. Other categories include professional, technical, and specialized services with obligations down to $24.1M."
